## 📚 QUICK REFERENCE

### Before creating a file:
- Is it a core file? → Check `AGENT-BEHAVIOR.mdc` (Core Files section)
- Is it documentation/summary/plan? → Require explicit user request
- Unsure? → ASK USER FIRST

### Before git operation:
- Verify branch aligns with task requirements (see `GIT-WORKFLOW.mdc` - Target Branch Determination)
- Verify files (core files only)
- All git operations are fully automated (see `CORE-AUTOMATION.mdc`)
- Never assume permission (but automation is default)

### Before completing work:
- Verify all checklist items (see `BEST-PRACTICES.mdc` - Compliance Checklist)
- Verify branch and files
- Verify no rules violated
- Verify PR branch deleted and PR closed (only main and beta remain)

